    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **270 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp08Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented registration-date defaulting for owners. When an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `Owner` schema. The OpenAPI generator regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `LocalDate registrationDate` field, and MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n3. **`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe design mirrors the existing `Visit.date` field (same OpenAPI `format: date` \u2192 `LocalDate` pattern), so it fits the surrounding conventions.",
